cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use calque in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "calque: run Modal-shaped code at AWS scale, unchanged"
abstract: >-
  calque is a structure-preserving translation layer that runs Modal-idiom
  Python scripts unchanged at AWS scale: the same script that runs over a
  handful of items on Modal runs over millions on AWS, without a logic
  rewrite. It widens its supported Modal-idiom surface toward real-world
  scripts, and surfaces anything it doesn't yet support as a structured leak
  rather than silently dropping semantics. Part of the spore.host suite.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Scott
    family-names: Friedman
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-1480-765X"
    affiliation: "Amazon Web Services"
repository-code: "https://github.com/spore-host/calque"
url: "https://spore.host"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - cloud computing
  - AWS
  - EC2
  - Modal
  - machine learning
  - GPU
